{"availability":"available","full":"EricEisaman/scs","name":"scs","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":15,"forks":5,"created":"2026-09-20T19:29:49Z","updated":"2026-10-11T05:41:25Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://ericeisaman.github.io/scs/PROCAUDIO.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.125Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.125Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.125Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.125Z","stars":15,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fast, faithful, Brython-powered implementation of the CMU Graphics API that runs in the browser. No server-side Python backend is required; scientific-computing labs load Pyodide and SciPy in a Web Worker when needed.","SCS is a drop-in browser runtime for CMU Graphics / cmugraphics coursework. You write the same onAppStart, onStep, redrawAll, onMousePress code you would in CMU Academy, and it runs on an HTML canvas via Brython.","1. Strict MVC, zero cheating Extensions are Model-only. They never import scs, never touch canvas, never draw. They fetch data. Your Controller (onAppStart, onMousePress) stores it in app.. Your View (redrawAll) reads app. and renders. CPCS-approved separation."],"features":["scs.py: the full API shim (Rect, Oval, Circle, Label, Line, Polygon, Group, Image, Sound, draw, rgb(), gradient(), distance(), angleTo(), etc.) with align as a true general property","index.html: production viewer. Loads apps from apps/ via URL param ?app=, with auto-start and a window.fetch loader","sandbox.html: live editor. Edit code in a textarea and hit Run. It also auto-starts","extensions/: NEW: SCS Extensions System, pure Model-layer libraries that bring the browser to your CMU app","apps/: all runnable apps. No root duplication."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/EricEisaman/scs/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint